§§ `s 2023(a) paragraphs (13) to (18) judicial review`

-- src:1874 | (13) If the store, concern, or State agency feels aggrieved by such final determination, it may obtain judicial review thereof by filing a complaint against the United States in the United States court for the district in which it resides or is engaged in business, or, in the case of a retail food store or wholesale food concern, in any court of record of the State having competent jurisdiction, within thirty days after the date of delivery or service of the final notice of determination upon it, requesting the court to set aside such determination.
@ref s 2023(a)(13) an aggrieved store, concern or State agency may obtain judicial review by filing a complaint within thirty days after delivery or service of the final notice (src:1874)
-- In plain words: a store, concern or State agency aggrieved by the final determination may sue the United States to have it set aside, if it files within thirty days after the final notice was delivered or served. The thirtieth day counts.
GIVEN `the store, concern, or State agency feels aggrieved by the final determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the delivery or service of the final notice of determination` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the complaint is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2023(a)(13) the complaint was filed in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the store, concern, or State agency feels aggrieved by the final determination` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the store, concern, or State agency feels aggrieved by such final determination"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date on which the complaint is filed` AT MOST Day `the date of the delivery or service of the final notice of determination` PLUS 30 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within thirty days after the date of delivery or service of the final notice of determination upon it"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1874 | (13) If the store, concern, or State agency feels aggrieved by such final determination, it may obtain judicial review thereof by filing a complaint against the United States in the United States court for the district in which it resides or is engaged in business, or, in the case of a retail food store or wholesale food concern, in any court of record of the State having competent jurisdiction, within thirty days after the date of delivery or service of the final notice of determination upon it, requesting the court to set aside such determination.
@ref s 2023(a)(13) the courts in which the complaint may be filed (src:1874)
-- In plain words: the complaint goes in the United States court for the district where the filer resides or is engaged in business; a retail food store or wholesale food concern may instead file in any court of record of a State having competent jurisdiction.
GIVEN `the party filing` IS A Party
      `the court is the United States court for the district in which the party resides or is engaged in business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is a court of record of the State having competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2023(a)(13) the complaint may be filed in the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court is the United States court for the district in which the party resides or is engaged in business` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the court is a court of record of the State having competent jurisdiction` AND (`the party filing` EQUALS `a retail food store` OR `the party filing` EQUALS `a wholesale food concern`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the United States court for the district in which it resides or is engaged in business, or, in the case of a retail food store or wholesale food concern, in any court of record of the State having competent jurisdiction"
            -- note (the list of courts is not closed with "only", so a court it does not name is not thereby barred)
            NOTHING

