§§ `s 2023(b) restoration of wrongfully withheld allotments`

-- In plain words: in a court case under the chapter, allotments found wrongfully withheld are restored only for periods of not more than one year before (i) the day the action began; or, if the action reviews a final State agency decision, (ii) the day a request for restoration was filed with the State;
-- or, in either case, (iii) the day the State agency was notified or found out about the possible loss. The text joins the three with "or". The module reads them as alternatives: restoration may reach back as far as the earliest of the limits that apply (NOTES.md, fork F-2023-1).
-- src:1881 | (b) In any judicial action arising under this chapter, any allotments found to have been wrongfully withheld shall be restored only for periods of not more than one year prior to the date of the commencement of such action, or in the case of an action seeking review of a final State agency determination, not more than one year prior to the date of the filing of a request with the State for the restoration of such allotments or, in either case, not more than one year prior to the date the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers the possible loss to a household.
@ref s 2023(b) the earliest date from which wrongfully withheld allotments are restored (src:1881)
GIVEN `the date of the commencement of the action` IS A DATE
      `the action seeks review of a final State agency determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the filing of a request with the State for the restoration of the allotments` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers the possible loss to the household` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2023(b) the earliest date from which allotments may be restored` MEANS
    `the earliest of the limits` WHERE
        `the limit from the commencement of the action` MEANS Day (`add years` `the date of the commencement of the action` (0 MINUS 1))
        `the limit from the request to the State` MEANS
            IF `the action seeks review of a final State agency determination`
            THEN
                CONSIDER `the date of the filing of a request with the State for the restoration of the allotments`
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the limit from the commencement of the action`
                    WHEN JUST requested THEN Day (`add years` requested (0 MINUS 1))
            ELSE `the limit from the commencement of the action`
        `the limit from the discovery of the loss` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers the possible loss to the household`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `the limit from the commencement of the action`
                WHEN JUST discovered THEN Day (`add years` discovered (0 MINUS 1))
        `the earliest of the limits` MEANS Date (min `the limit from the commencement of the action` (min `the limit from the request to the State` `the limit from the discovery of the loss`))

-- src:1881 | (b) In any judicial action arising under this chapter, any allotments found to have been wrongfully withheld shall be restored only for periods of not more than one year prior to the date of the commencement of such action, or in the case of an action seeking review of a final State agency determination, not more than one year prior to the date of the filing of a request with the State for the restoration of such allotments or, in either case, not more than one year prior to the date the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers the possible loss to a household.
@ref s 2023(b) allotments may be restored for a period beginning on the date (src:1881)
GIVEN `the date of the commencement of the action` IS A DATE
      `the action seeks review of a final State agency determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the filing of a request with the State for the restoration of the allotments` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers the possible loss to the household` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the first day of the period for which restoration is sought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2023(b) the allotments may be restored for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the first day of the period for which restoration is sought` AT LEAST Day (`s 2023(b) the earliest date from which allotments may be restored` `the date of the commencement of the action` `the action seeks review of a final State agency determination` `the date of the filing of a request with the State for the restoration of the allotments` `the date the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers the possible loss to the household`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be restored only for periods of not more than one year prior to the date of the commencement of such action"
            JUST FALSE
